  "changed_since_previous": "No functional changes; diff is now available confirming the implementation from closed PR #36355 and the added functional test.",
  "card": "This pull request stops the HTTP server from processing pipelined requests queued after a connection-closing reply and forces connection closure on conflicting framing headers (Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding). Introduced as a regression from the libevent replacement in #35182, buffered requests currently execute even after a closing reply, violating RFC 9112 sections 6.1 and 9.6 and allowing trailing pipelined RPC commands like setnetworkactive false to run unexpectedly. The PR introduces an atomic closing state flag to stop further reads and adds unit and functional regression tests. It has no open dependencies.",
